From 9861e3afc4669f88a4a97cccded3ed30f26bb261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: migrate index storage and merge operations to MDBX

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics. The candidate repair below
changes this boundary and requires new validation evidence.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add the libmdbx CDBWrapper and Chronik storage backend with automatic migration
from legacy LevelDB and RocksDB databases.

Original-Commit: be9d70e3f86dd845b57ba15fa9568529957247e6
Original-Patch: ecash/004
Split-Concern: chronik-db

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Replace the unsafe pseudo-migration (backup files then return an empty index) with explicit refusal before any MDBX creation when RocksDB or backup artifacts exist. Preserve file bytes, add data-preservation regressions, and retain the regenerated Cargo.lock. Actual RocksDB key/value migration is not implemented or claimed; fresh MDBX indexes remain supported.

Plan-v2 owner repair: C: preserve legacy-artifact refusal with actionable original-data guidance and Rust regression. Startup resynchronization remains synchronous; the documented STOP condition is retained.

